{"id":"word:hebrew:H8518","type":"word","title":"תָּלָה","subtitle":"H8518 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to suspend (especially to gibbet)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to תָּלָה (H8518) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 29 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"תָּלָה (tâlâh) means to suspend (especially to gibbet) First listed occurrence: 2Sam 4 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"תָּלָה","transliteration":"tâlâh","pronunciation":"taw-law'","strong":"H8518","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8518","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יִּתְל֥וּ","תָּל֖וּי","תלו/ם","תְּלָא֥וּ/ם","וְ/תָלִ֥יתָ"],"morphs":[["HVqsmsa",3],["HVqp3ms",3],["HC/Vqw3mp",2],["HVqp3cp/Sp3mp",2],["HR/Vqc",2],["HVqp3cp",2],["HC/Vqq3cp",2],["HVpp3cp",2],["HC/Vqq2ms",1],["HC/VNw3mp",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to suspend (especially to gibbet)","usage":"hang (up).","full":"H8518. talah תָּלָה verb hang (Late Hebrew id. ; Assyrian Pi`el tullû , hang up ; Arabic let down, dangle (a rope, etc.); Aramaic תְּלָא , hang ; perhaps Old Aramaic תלה id. , Lzb 386 ; Ethiopic in derived sense, be devoted, addicted, to ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳ת Gen 40:22 +; 2 masculine singular וְתָלִ֫יתָ Deut 21:22 consecutive; 3 plural תָּלוּ Est 8:7 ; 9:14 suffix תלום 2Sam 21:12 Kt (Qr see תלא ), etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular suffix וַיִּתְלֵם Josh 10:26 , etc.; Imperative masculine plural suffix תְּלֻהוּ Est 7:9 ; Infinitive construct לִתְלוֺת Ezek 15:3 ; Est 6:4 ; Participle active תֹּלֶה Job 26:7 ; passive תָּלוּי Deut 31:23 2 t., plural תְּלוּיִם Josh 10:26 ; &#8212; hang: 1 hang up any object: accusative of hands and feet of slain, + עַלהַֿבְּרֵכָה 2Sam 4:12 ; תָּלוּי of Absalom בָּאֵלָה in the terebinth 18:10 ; ׳ת with accusative of thing, + עַל Isa 22:24 ; Ezek 15:3 ; Song 4:4 ; Psa 137:2 ; subject ׳ת עַלבְּֿלִימָה אֶרֶץ ׳י, Job 26:7 . 2 specifically put to death by hanging , with accusative of person Gen 40:22 ; 41:13 (both E), 2Sam 21:12 (compare תלא ), Est 9:14 ; absolute תָּלוּי Deut 21:23 one hanged ; accusative of person + עַלעֵֿץ Gen 40:19 (E), Deut 21:22 ; Josh 8:29 ; 10:26 (twice in verse) (all J E), Est 5:14 ; 6:4 ; 7:9-10 , 8:7 ; 9:13 , 25 . Niph`al Perfect 3plural נִתְלוּ בְּיָדָם שָׂרִים Lam 5:12 princes have been hung up by their hands; Imperfect 3masculine plural עַלעֵֿץ וַיִּתָּלוּ Est 2:23 they were hanged on a tree ; + 3 masculine singular with apocope וַיִּתָּל 2Sam 18:9 (for וַיּתַֻּן see נתן Hoph`al ). Pi`el hang up for display, with accusative of thing: Perfect 3plural תִּלּוּ Ezek 27:10 ( ב location), 27:11 ( עַלאחוֺמוֺתַיִךְ ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Sam 4 12","keyReferences":["2Sam 4 12","2Sam 18 10","2Sam 21 12","2Sam 21 12","Deut 21 22","Deut 21 23","Esth 2 23","Esth 5 14"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":29,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Sam 4 12","book":"2Sam","chapter":4,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּתְל֥וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"2Sam 18 10","book":"2Sam","chapter":18,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תָּל֖וּי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqsmsa"},{"reference":"2Sam 21 12","book":"2Sam","chapter":21,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תלו/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3cp/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"2Sam 21 12","book":"2Sam","chapter":21,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תְּלָא֥וּ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3cp/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"Deut 21 22","book":"Deut","chapter":21,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/תָלִ֥יתָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq2ms"},{"reference":"Deut 21 23","book":"Deut","chapter":21,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תָּל֑וּי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqsmsa"},{"reference":"Esth 2 23","book":"Esth","chapter":2,"verse":